    "body": "Quick pass (coordinator, read only, no build) on head `7b645e188`: the PR is a sub-PR of `side/path-kernel` and merges cleanly with it (`7f70d8b1a`). The author's gate is green on this head: `cargo check --tests` for pathkernel and motion, the `laws` suite (130 passed), the motion `kernel_laws` suite (30 passed), clippy, the quick gate against the side branch (4 steps), the three example catalog suites and the light lane (7 steps). The writer record on #4026 is released. The body starts with `Side branch: side/path-kernel` and has `Refs #4026`. The PR is flagged ready. It waits for the independent review.\n\nNotes for the reviewer. The safety floor applies: this stage decides how much the tool cuts.\n- A known gap of this PR: for the material side Outside, the motion reading has over-limit moves with no name (74 on the disc, 66 on the dog bone), all on the stock edge line. That breaks law 6 at that place. The author filed #4260 for it. Decide if the PR can merge with this gap or if the fix belongs in this PR.\n- The stage does not reach a constant engagement. With load control, the worst reading for Inside is still 173 degrees (the first ring round the part, named), and the trochoidal mode reads 0.941 on the neck (it was 1.0). Check that each cut over the limit that stays is named, and that the readings in the body agree with the pins.\n- The author found that its first engagement reader read about 10 degrees too low and changed it to read as the motion meter does. Check the reader against the published law that it cites.\n- `Reach::Stock` (Adaptive) is refused by name in this stage. Check that this agrees with the design record (Offset rings and Adaptive stay two names).\n- The trial merge and the gate base are `origin/side/path-kernel`. PR #4253 (the link proof) and PR #4244 (guide planners, refresh in work) are open at the same time.",
